{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum cycle basis (de Pina 1995): "},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cycles, for c"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, independent over GF(2) and spanning the cycle space, with the fewest edges in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"total of any such basis. Self-loops and parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its own, and two copies of an edge form a cycle of length 2. Each cycle starts at its least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cycles come in nondecreasing length, then by their edge positions. Ties between equally"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"short cycles are broken by the rows’ order."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcyclebasis()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCycleBasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Cycle","text":"Cycle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdent